1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,100
You have been alone on this barren rock

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:06,340
in the Atlantic Ocean for an entire month.

3
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:10,780
No visitors, no escape from the endless crash

4
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:11,480
of the surf.

5
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:15,920
You are the sole lighthouse keeper, bound to

6
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:17,100
a single duty.

7
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:21,060
Keep the beam burning so passing ships survive

8
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:21,760
the dark.

9
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:23,640
Until tonight.

10
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:27,140
A violent gale hammers the stone tower.

11
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:29,940
You finish trimming the lamp wick and start

12
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:32,060
down the spiral iron staircase.

13
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:35,240
Then you freeze.

14
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:38,660
Above you, on the walkway you just left,

15
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:41,660
heavy footsteps pace the floorboards.

16
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:44,060
Slow, deliberate.

17
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:47,560
You raise your lantern and climb back up.

18
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:51,020
The room is empty, except for a storm

19
00:00:51,020 --> 00:00:53,440
hatch standing wide open to the driving rain.

20
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:55,960
You know you latched it minutes ago.

21
00:00:56,660 --> 00:00:59,700
You slam it shut, lock it tight, and

22
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:00,400
head back down.

23
00:01:01,460 --> 00:01:04,580
Instantly, the pacing starts again, directly over your

24
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:04,820
head.

25
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:08,380
The ceiling timbers creak under unmistakable weight.

26
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:11,680
Down in your quarters, you try to steady

27
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:12,180
your breath.

28
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:15,300
Then comes a sound that makes your blood

29
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:16,220
run cold.

30
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:19,660
Three sharp knocks on the front door.

31
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:23,040
Nobody lands a boat in seas like this.

32
00:01:23,880 --> 00:01:26,060
You take your lantern to the entrance and

33
00:01:26,060 --> 00:01:27,960
pull back the heavy iron bolt.

34
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:30,660
You swing the door open into the howling

35
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:31,060
gale.

36
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:32,420
Nothing.

37
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:35,060
Just churning black water.

38
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:38,680
Then your light catches the stone threshold.

39
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:40,760
Wet footprints.

40
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:45,060
Bare human feet, soaked in brine, leading straight

41
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:46,740
from the surf up to your boots.

42
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:48,640
None lead back out.

43
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:51,880
You slam the door shut and back away.

44
00:01:52,860 --> 00:01:56,280
Right behind your ear, a familiar voice whispers

45
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:56,960
your name.

46
00:01:57,640 --> 00:02:00,220
It belongs to someone you buried years ago.

47
00:02:01,020 --> 00:02:03,300
You bolt to the radio desk, flicking the

48
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:04,160
transmitter frantically.

49
00:02:04,580 --> 00:02:04,860
Mayday!

50
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:05,380
Mayday!

51
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:06,500
Lighthouse station!

52
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:07,520
Does anyone read?

53
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:09,320
Static hisses.

54
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:12,860
Then a calm voice answers through the speaker.

55
00:02:14,020 --> 00:02:15,520
Extinguish the light.

56
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:17,420
It sees you.

57
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:21,020
You turn slowly toward the seaward window.

58
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:24,760
Out among the cresting waves stands a dark

59
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:28,260
silhouette, perfectly motionless on the churning water.

60
00:02:29,060 --> 00:02:31,040
You blink, and it vanishes.

61
00:02:32,340 --> 00:02:36,400
Suddenly, the main lighthouse beam dies pitch black.

62
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:39,400
The backup generator kicks in, and in the

63
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:41,920
glass pane before you, you see a pale

64
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:44,700
face reflected right over your shoulder.

65
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:46,960
You whip around, swinging blindly.

66
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:48,500
The room is empty.

67
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:50,600
Panic takes over.

68
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:52,500
You run for the exit, tearing the door

69
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:52,820
open.

70
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:56,420
But the gale has died into an unnatural,

71
00:02:56,860 --> 00:02:58,040
suffocating fog.

72
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,820
A voice whispers from the white mist.

73
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:04,760
Before you can move, cold breath hits the

74
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:05,500
side of your neck.

75
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:08,120
What took you so long?

76
00:03:09,140 --> 00:03:11,720
Before you can move, cold breath hits the

77
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:12,500
side of your neck.

78
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:14,760
You were never alone.

79
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:18,180
Every bulb in the tower shatters.

80
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:22,700
In the blackness, heavy glass crashes on the

81
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:23,480
top floor.

82
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:28,160
You strike a match, relight your lantern, and

83
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:29,980
mount the spiral stairs.

84
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:34,140
With every step you take, a second set

85
00:03:34,140 --> 00:03:36,960
of footsteps follows directly behind you.

86
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:38,320
Clang.

87
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:40,880
You reach the upper doorway.

88
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:44,940
The rusted door slowly swings open into the

89
00:03:44,940 --> 00:03:45,240
dark.

90
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:49,540
From inside the gloom, a voice speaks.

91
00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:50,960
Smooth.

92
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:52,320
Calm.

93
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:54,760
It is your own voice.

94
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:56,960
Come inside.

95
00:03:57,760 --> 00:04:01,300
You are frozen in the hallway, listening to

96
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:03,700
your own mouth speak from the dark.

97
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:07,080
Your lantern flame abruptly snuffs out.

98
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:10,340
A sharp gasp cuts the silence, then a

99
00:04:10,340 --> 00:04:12,980
scream that rattles the iron frame of the

100
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:13,260
tower.

101
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:16,760
Then, absolute stillness.

102
00:04:18,339 --> 00:04:21,420
Days later, a relief tender arrives under clear

103
00:04:21,420 --> 00:04:21,900
skies.

104
00:04:22,540 --> 00:04:24,860
They find the lighthouse cold and abandoned.

105
00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:26,800
The kettle sits on the stove.

106
00:04:27,260 --> 00:04:28,380
The radio is off.

107
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:31,300
Your lantern lies shattered at the base of

108
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:31,740
the stairs.

109
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:35,080
They search the cliffs, the rocks, the shoreline.

110
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:36,760
No trace of a body.

111
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:40,080
Then the crew climbs to the top storeroom.

112
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:43,420
The storm window is bolted tight from the

113
00:04:43,420 --> 00:04:46,640
inside, and across the dusty floor runs a

114
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:48,680
trail of damp seawater footprints.

115
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:51,540
They begin out of nowhere, in the middle

116
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:53,760
of the room, lead straight to the glass,

117
00:04:54,340 --> 00:04:54,940
and stop.

118
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,100
No tracks coming in.

119
00:04:57,740 --> 00:04:58,840
No tracks leaving.

120
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:02,300
Some claim the solitude broke you and you

121
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:05,080
jumped, but that will never explain a window

122
00:05:05,080 --> 00:05:06,440
locked from the inside.

123
00:05:07,020 --> 00:05:09,580
And it will never explain the voice that

124
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:10,540
answered the radio.

125
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:13,240
The lighthouse still stands.

126
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:16,920
Tonight, you can almost hear three sharp knocks

127
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:19,900
against the glass, eighty feet above the sea.

128
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:23,880
The radio clicks on by itself, and your

129
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:25,200
own voice whispers.

130
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:29,920
Whisper child, it's your turn to keep the

131
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:30,620
light burning.
